cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Manana or Bayesian prompt averaging, please cite the NeurIPS 2026 paper below."
title: "Manana: Teaching LLMs to Recommend and Defer in Underrepresented Epilepsy Care"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/roychowdhuryresearch/Manana"
url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.31036"
abstract: >-
  Manana is an LLM clinical decision-support framework for anti-seizure medication
  prescribing, studied on pediatric epilepsy care in Uganda with longitudinal clinic
  notes from two independently collected cohorts. It learns local prescribing
  guidance from a small patient-level training set by turning prescription errors
  into auditable prompt memory, with single-agent and multi-agent variants. Bayesian
  prompt averaging (BPA) combines predictions across the learned prompt trajectory
  to produce prescription likelihoods and a deferral signal, so lower-confidence
  cases can be routed to specialists.
keywords:
  - clinical decision support
  - large language models
  - medication recommendation
  - learning to defer
  - selective prediction
  - uncertainty calibration
  - prompt learning
  - multi-agent systems
  - global health
  - epilepsy
